erson_slug":"nigel-scullion","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nova Peris","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10820","person_slug":"nova-peris","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Robert Simms","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10842","person_slug":"robert-simms","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Education Services for Overseas Students Amendment (Streamlining Regulation) Bill 2015 and one other - in Committee - Keeping fees in separate account","noes":30,"question":"The majority voted in favour of [amendment (1)](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2015-11-30.164.1), introduced by Labor Senator [Kim Carr](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/kim_carr). This means the amendment was successful, though it still needs to be agreed to by the members of the House of Representatives before it can be included in [the bill](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r5544) (read more about the [process of making amendments in Parliament](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/amendments.html)). ### What is the amendment? The amendment relates to item 3 of schedule 5, which says: > *Division 2 deals with tuition fees. In general, a registered provider must not receive more than 50% of the total tuition fees for a course before an overseas student begins the course.* The amendment proposed to add the following words: '*The provider must keep those fees in a separate account*' into item 3 or Schedule 5. Senator Carr [explains that this amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2015-11-30.164.1) has been introduced to reduce financial risk to the [Tuition Protection Service](https://tps.gov.au/Home/NotLoggedIn), which assists students who are struggling to get a refund where their education provider cannot deliver their course. ### What do these bills do? These bills amend the [Educational Services for Overseas Students regulatory framework](https://internationaleducation.gov.au/regulatory-information/pages/regulatoryinformation.aspx), which has three main objectives: * '*to provide tuition assurance, and refunds, for overseas students for courses for which they have paid and* * *to protect and enhance Australia’s reputation for quality education and training services and* * *to complement Australia’s migration laws by ensuring providers collect and report information relevant to the administration of the law relating to student visas.*' Read more in th","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4007","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-11-30/2"}
